+## Acceptance criteria
+- `median` is defined in `mathkit/stats.py` and importable as `from mathkit import median`.
+- Odd count returns the middle value of the sorted input.
+- Even count returns the mean of the two middle values as a float.
+- An empty sequence (list or empty iterator) raises ValueError.
+- The input is not mutated.
+- Any iterable is accepted (list, tuple, set, generator).
+- `tests/test_stats.py` covers each behavior above.
+- `README.md` gains exactly one line describing `median`.
+- `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` passes.
+- Only the four files in Context are changed (plus this handoff's acceptance criteria); standard library only.
